================================================================================
SIS-POLICY LANGUAGE
================================================================================

GENERAL DESIGN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SIS-Policy is:

• Declarative (like SELinux)
• Readable (simpler than SELinux)
• Modular (policy modules can extend rules)
• Deterministic
• Event-driven
• Capability-based

Core idea:

    allow / deny / require / audit / quarantine

No complex macro language required.

================================================================================
POLICY STRUCTURE
================================================================================

policy "system-default" {

    version: 1

    profile: "high-security"

    default {
        service: deny
        device: deny
        network: deny
    }

    rules {

        allow service if service.signed == true
        allow service if service.capability <= allowed_capabilities

        allow network if service.requires_network == true
        deny network if usb.malicious == true

        require usb.storage -> signed_device == true
        require network.tor if service.tag == "anonymous"

        audit service.start
        audit policy.violation

        quarantine service if service.crash_count > 3

    }
}
