DESIGN GOALS OF SIS-POLICY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Simpler than SELinux
• More readable than AppArmor
• More modular than either
• Fully deterministic
• Policy-driven security model
• Central enforcement point
• No hidden enforcement logic
• Easily auditable rules
• Extensible by modules

================================================================================
LONG-TERM VISION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SIS becomes:

• A minimal init core
• A modular operating system control plane
• A unified security enforcement layer
• A policy-driven service orchestration system

Instead of many disconnected systems (SELinux, systemd units, udev rules,
firewalls, VPN logic), SIS-Policy becomes the single declarative layer that
describes:

    "What is allowed to exist and under what conditions"

